{
  "version": "1.2.6",
  "published": "2026-11-07",
  "changelog": [
    "**Nothing is see-through any more.** 1.2.5 shipped every inflatable body inside-out: the game draws only the outside of a surface, so it skipped the near side and showed the far side from within. A bride's hair showed through her face, the elephant's trunk looked hollow, balloons looked like bowls. The builder now winds every surface outward and refuses to write a model that is not.",
    "**Boxes and cylinders.** The builder only knew rounded blobs, so anything square or round-sided came out as a lump. It now builds real boxes and cylinders, and these were redesigned with them: the **gingerbread house** (walls, a gable, two icing roof slabs, chimney, door, windows with panes, gumdrops along the eaves), the **stack of presents** (wrapped boxes, ribbon both ways, bows), the **Christmas train** (boiler, stack, cab with windows, cowcatcher, gold wheels, a tender of presents), the **dreidel** (a square body on its point, a handle, a Hebrew letter on each face), the **Uncle Sam hat** (a tall striped crown, starred band, brim), both **cakes** (round tiers with icing and drips), the **champagne toast** (two flutes leaning in), and the **barbecue grill** (kettle on three legs, grate with burgers and hot dogs, lid open behind).",
    "**Redesigned to look like the product:** the **black cat** sits up with green eyes, whiskers, a collar and bell and a tail curled round its paws (it was a blob on four paddles); the **cat on the pumpkin** is the same cat; the **haunted tree** is a dark gnarled trunk with roots, a face and branches that bend up and out; the **cornucopia** is a proper horn with a dark mouth and a pile of harvest in front; the **rainbow arch** is six smooth bands (it was rows of beads); the **gold star** has a stand.",
    "**Strings and thin parts** (balloon strings, cupid's bow string) no longer come out as dashes.",
    "**A quarter of the triangles, the same look.** Every model is simplified after it is built; the `stream` folder went from 51 MB to 22 MB and the download is a third smaller. Same model names: everything already placed updates in place.",
    "**The bunny's and the chick's eyes** were inside their heads. Any feature that would be buried in the skin is now moved out to the surface.",
    "**Downloads are retried and paced.** The updater fired every file at once (300 of them) and a server updating from 1.0 lost two to GitHub and gave up with \"2 files could not be verified\" and no names. Six at a time now, three tries each.",
    "**Failures say which files and why**, in game and in the console, whether a download failed (try again), a file did not match the manifest (report it), or a file needs a folder the old version never had (the message names the folder to create; a 1.0 server needs `audio/sfx`)."
  ],
